  "notes": "Soul/gospel-rasp pop with a live rhythm section. The entry states the feel rather than the tempo class first — \"backbeat on 2&4 straight, frequently in a 12/8 or swung-16th soul feel\" — so `halfTime` is false at `backbeat_24` and `swing.amount` is 0.6 on a 16th grid, which is this author's reading of \"swung-16th\" and is disclosed as such. The kit is the entry's: \"played soul kit with a fat backbeat, ghost-noted 16ths on the snare, and tambourine on offbeats; handclaps in the final chorus. Programmed layers sit under the live kit on the pop-facing singles.\" So the ghost map is dense at four positions, `tambourine` sits at `offbeat`, and the humanize block is a played one with real jitter on every lane. No `bass808` block: \"no 808. Fingered electric bass with a walking soul line; organ pedal reinforcing the root\", which is `independent_riff` at 0.38 with a full walking passing-tone set. Harmony is \"4- or 8-bar loops\" of \"minor and major with gospel passing chords and a plagal cadence\", so the IV—I family sits at top weight beside a ii—V—I and the seventh/ninth share is high — gospel harmony is not triadic. Melody encodes \"melisma-heavy with blues-third bends, building from a low conversational register to a rasped belt\" as `colorTones` on the flat third and seventh, an arch contour, a wide register and `endVariation`; \"backing is a gospel-style choir stack\" is `sustain_pad` at top weight. ⚠ `confidence` is medium and the research says \"tempo/harmony bands inferred\": `swing.amount` 0.6, every drum probability, the humanize numbers, the harmonic weights and `bpm.mode` 90 (the midpoint of the stated 80—100 core) are INFERRED, and the entry's [LOW-CONF] mark on the rasped baritone-tenor claim is repeated here.",
